comments.body:
Thanks for the review, y'all. 

@tristanls: I've made your suggested edits. I'm looking forward to seeing/hearing more about tests and developing better practices.

@jeremyshoemaker: The decorator approach is pretty nice. I think if we were to do that, I'd probably make it a class method of `BufferEncoder` (`BufferEncoder.encodes`).  It's light years from being a priority, but it'd be nice if we had other formats available for logging someday (i.e., HDF5) since these JSON files are ~3-4x larger than they need to be and don't deserialize nicely. In which case, we'd also have `HDF5Encoder.encodes` or something like that.
